-- title:
--   Twisted Mumford tower over unramified quadratic coefficients
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O$ which is a domain, with $\pi$ irreducible, $\mathcal O$ complete for the $\pi$-adic topology, residue ring of cardinality $r$, and $(r)=(\pi)$; let $K_0$ be its fraction field. Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero domain over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, every element satisfying a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo it, every monic polynomial of positive degree having a root modulo it, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}$ modulo it. Let $v\!\det:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) satisfy $v\!\det g=n$ exactly when $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$. Let $G$ be a group, $\sigma:G\to\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, $\Gamma\le G$ containing an element $z$ with $\sigma z$ scalar and $v\!\det(\sigma z)=2$ and an element $w$ with $v\!\det(\sigma w)=1$, let $\Gamma'$ be the set of $x\in\Gamma$ with $v\!\det(\sigma x)$ even, and let $\rho:G\to\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ be induced by $\sigma$; assume $\rho(\Gamma')$ has finite stabilisers of, and finitely many orbits on, the vertices (homothety classes of full lattices) of the tree of $K_0$. Put $g_1=\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$, let $N\le\rho(\Gamma')$ be normal in $\rho(\Gamma)$ of finite relative index in $\rho(\Gamma')$, and let $DM$ be a `MumfordTower` $\mathcal O,\pi,K_0,r,g_1,N$, with levels $DM.Z\,n$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$, transitions $DM.zt$, and charts $DM.q\,n$ classifying Deligne data. Write $\mathcal O_2$ for the equaliser of $\mathrm{Fr}^2$ and the identity on $Onr$. Then there exist schemes $X_n$ with morphisms $xb_n:X_n\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$, transitions $xt_n:X_n\to X_{n+1}$, a finite group $G_2$ with homomorphisms $a_n:G_2\to\mathrm{Aut}(X_n)$, projections $pr_{1,n}:X_n\to DM.Z\,n$ and $pr_{2,n}:X_n\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_2/\pi^{n+1}$, a homomorphism $\theta:\Gamma\to G_2$ and $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphisms $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}$ of $\mathcal O_2/\pi^{n+1}$ such that: each transition square for $xt_n$ over the reduction $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+2}\to\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$ is cartesian; each $xb_n$ is proper and flat; every finite subset of $X_n$ lies in an affine open; each $a_n(g)$ commutes with $xb_n$ and with the transitions; $(pr_{1,n},pr_{2,n})$ exhibits $X_n$ as the fibre product of $DM.zb\,n$ with $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_2/\pi^{n+1}\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$, with $xb_n=pr_{1,n}$ followed by $DM.zb\,n$ and both projections compatible with the transitions; $\theta$ is surjective with $\theta\gamma=1$ iff $\rho\gamma\in N$; $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}$ is induced by $\mathrm{Fr}$ on residue classes; $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ acts on the coefficient factor through $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}^{-v\!\det(\sigma\gamma)}$; and for every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi^{n+1}=0$ in $B$ and Deligne data $P,P'$ over $B$ with $P'$ the pullback of $P$ along $\sigma(\gamma)^{-1}$ (levelwise comparison of the lines on each full lattice), any $x:\operatorname{Spec}B\to X_n$ with $pr_{1,n}\circ x=DM.q\,n\,B\,P$ satisfies $pr_{1,n}\circ a_n(\theta\gamma)\circ x=DM.q\,n\,B\,P'$.
--
--   This is the base change of a Mumford tower attached to a normal subgroup $N$ to the coefficients $\mathcal O_2=(Onr)^{\mathrm{Fr}^2}$, carrying an action of the finite quotient $\rho(\Gamma)/N$ that twists the coefficient factor by a power of Frobenius determined by the valuation of the determinant — the form in which the Čerednik–Drinfel'd uniformisation produces a quotient with its Galois descent data. It is used in the construction of a formal quotient datum with the required adic behaviour of the coefficients.
